From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 16:52:47 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 45/97] Plutonium: a parked window's popups show only where a
 page shows it

Menus and tooltips of a parked window were drawn over the shell even when
no page showed the window (another thread, or the panel closed). The
embedder now tells Exo whether a page shows the window, where, and at what
scale (EmbeddedWindows::SetShown()). Its popups follow: shown nowhere, they
stay open but invisible, take no real input and hold no pointer grab;
shown, they move with the window to where the page shows it and are scaled
with it about the window's origin.
